WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.916
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.418 --> 00:00:08.460
CY KHORMAEE: My name is
Cy, I'm a product manager

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:09.900
with Google Cloud.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.863
And with that,
let's get into it.

00:00:13.863 --> 00:00:15.780
So I think hopefully
most of folks in the room

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.310
are security or
security adjacent

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.550
have some experience with the
problems of protecting users.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.890
You knoqm users are under
attack from phishing, malware,

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.250
and fraud at all times.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.958
And it's really unique compared
to protecting our own employees

00:00:27.958 --> 00:00:30.000
because we have less
control over the environment

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.420
in which our users exist.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.510
But they're just as
important to our business.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.160
You know, with
phishing, you know,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.470
91% of all targeted attacks
start with phishing.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.880
That's one huge vector in
not only to your own systems,

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.900
but to your customers
and your users.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.330
And 8% of revenue for
many online businesses

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:48.968
is lost to fraud every year.

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:51.010
The problem is just the
defense of these systems,

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:53.790
especially you go all the way
out to the users' computers,

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.890
requires a lot of
data and the ability

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.050
to protect at the client
level in an environment

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.087
that you don't control.

00:01:00.087 --> 00:01:02.420
Now, just for some background,
you know, here at Google,

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:03.962
we've been protecting
our own systems

00:01:03.962 --> 00:01:06.850
with two spectacular
platforms for the last decade,

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:08.840
and maybe even
more in some cases.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:10.300
The first is Safe
Browsing, which

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.040
defends over three
billion devices

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:14.207
from phishing and malware.

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:15.790
And then the other
is reCAPTCHA, which

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:17.410
defends more than
two million websites

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.210
from fraudulently using bots.

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:21.610
And we really took
these two platforms

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:24.640
and leveraged them to create
offerings that you all can now

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.910
use in order to protect your
own platforms users and devices.

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:31.913
The first of these products
is reCAPTCHA Enterprise.

00:01:31.913 --> 00:01:33.580
Now, reCAPTCHA
Enterprise is essentially

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:37.630
an extension of reCAPTCHA
V3 into the enterprise space

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:40.510
to allow for more nuance
and granular control

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:42.700
and smarter and more
refined decision

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.740
making around what to
do with fraud that you

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:47.060
observe on your site.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:48.977
The second two are based
off of Safe Browsing.

00:01:48.977 --> 00:01:50.977
The first one there will
be phishing protection,

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:53.500
which essentially leverages
the power of Safe Browsing

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.490
to discover phishing sites that
are targeting your company.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:00.190
To add those, help you get
those added to Safe Browsing

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:02.350
as well as enable you
to potentially submit

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:05.500
your own URLs you observed
to be attacking your users

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:06.958
to save browsing.

00:02:06.958 --> 00:02:09.250
And then the third product
we'll introduce is Web Risk.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:10.930
And Web Risk is a
URL, again, built

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.640
on the power of
Safe Browsing that

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:15.700
enables you to check URLs
in your own infrastructure

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.965
on your own site in the content
that you serve for unsafe URLs.

00:02:19.965 --> 00:02:22.090
And with that, we'll do a
little bit of a deep dive

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:23.440
in each one of these here.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.050
We'll start out here with
reCAPTCHA Enterprise,

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:27.670
and really wanted
to kind of frame

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:30.640
the problem of how we see a lot
of what we think of reCAPTCHA

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:32.860
is just defending against
bots, which it does,

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:35.650
but it also defends against all
different manner of attacks.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:39.370
And this could be scraping
fraudulent transactions,

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:42.010
account takeovers, synthetic
accounts, false posts, money

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:43.690
laundering, and many, many more.

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:48.130
I'm never cease to be amazed by
the creativity and innovation

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:49.973
of our adversaries.

00:02:49.973 --> 00:02:51.640
So there are just
this myriad of threats

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:52.890
that try and abuse your sites.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:55.330
And really the goal
with the reCAPTCHA,

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:57.070
and reCAPTCHA
enterprise, specifically,

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:58.750
is to make it as
hard as possible

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:01.990
for these adversaries to
access anything on your site,

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:04.218
be it the login page
or even your home page,

00:03:04.218 --> 00:03:06.760
and make it as easy as possible,
and in fact, as frictionless

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:10.210
as possible for your own users
to engage with and conduct

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.428
legitimate business
on your site.

00:03:12.428 --> 00:03:13.720
Now how are we able to do that?

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:16.840
You know, reCAPTCHA really
has an unprecedented level

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:21.100
of visibility of abuse across
the web from the two million

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.100
sites that we work with.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:25.270
And we're able to kind of
combine all these collective,

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:29.020
collaborative defenses to
create a unique view on what

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:31.450
legitimate and what
illegitimate transactions look

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:34.178
like across this large
population, which it enables us

00:03:34.178 --> 00:03:35.720
to train machine
learning models that

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:39.850
are able to recognize attacks in
their many and evolving forms.

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:41.770
And speaking of evolving,
I want to walk you

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:43.620
through a quick history of
our reCAPTCHA to bring you up

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:44.560
to speed because
I think people's

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.930
understanding of this platform
vary because it's just been

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:48.722
around for so long and
has been experienced

00:03:48.722 --> 00:03:50.943
by so many different
people in different ways.

00:03:50.943 --> 00:03:53.110
Really, it got started with
the squiggly bit of text

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:55.900
that you're trying
to read and type in.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:00.380
And as bots got better,
our defenses had to evolve.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.430
And that's why you see these
click boxes and crosswalks

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.340
where the challenges have become
a little bit more complex.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:09.575
And I know many people in the
audience, myself included--

00:04:09.575 --> 00:04:10.450
can't touch the mic--

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:13.910
have trouble solving.

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:15.743
And the reason they've
gotten so complicated

00:04:15.743 --> 00:04:17.829
is not only just
because of the AI threat

00:04:17.829 --> 00:04:19.660
but also because of
the farmer threat.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:21.970
So there are large groups
of, even warehouses full,

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:24.140
of people who are
solving these challenges.

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:27.220
So the threat is in fact a human
threat as well as a bot threat.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:29.110
And we really have
to distinguish

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:31.240
legitimate from
fraudulent transactions

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.670
not just bots from
humans anymore.

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:35.560
Not to mention that AI
get smarter every day,

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:38.552
and maybe those will converge
with the human threat.

00:04:38.552 --> 00:04:40.760
And so really that brought
us to this, which you know

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.040
is nothing.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:42.760
Just kidding.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.860
So really what it is a
piece of JavaScript that

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:47.890
can live almost anywhere on
your site, anywhere on the web,

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:49.480
interact with the
user, and give you

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:51.160
essentially a risk
or a confidence

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:53.410
score in whether
this interaction's

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:55.890
fraudulent or not, without
interrupting your user,

00:04:55.890 --> 00:05:01.810
and without being easily tested
or defeated by a piece of AI

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:04.390
or a bot written
by an adversary.

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:05.890
And really this is
our effort to go

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:07.570
into the behavioral
analytic space

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:10.572
and really try and use not just
the challenge but, in fact,

00:05:10.572 --> 00:05:12.280
everything you can
observe about the user

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:14.110
from their interaction
on the client

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:15.627
in order to make
a determination.

00:05:15.627 --> 00:05:17.710
Again, that's not only
better for users in that it

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:18.868
causes zero user friction.

00:05:18.868 --> 00:05:20.410
In fact, most users
aren't even aware

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:23.830
that they are passing this test.

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:27.400
But it also is much harder to
defeat because the adversaries

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:30.280
don't have a strong idea of what
they have to program against

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:34.390
or a way to train
their own attacks.

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:36.940
And now with the reCAPTCHA
enterprise, what we found

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.475
is that with the
introduction of E3,

00:05:38.475 --> 00:05:39.850
you can put the
snippet anywhere,

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:42.230
which means that you have a
much broader set of use cases

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:43.480
around where you can use this.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.880
I think in V2, a lot of
the common use cases we saw

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:47.290
was around the login flow.

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:49.480
When there's already going
to be a user interaction

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:51.190
and already interrupt
there, we can

00:05:51.190 --> 00:05:53.812
add a little bit of extra
friction keep it secure.

00:05:53.812 --> 00:05:55.270
Now with a frictionless
experience,

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:56.812
you can put it
anywhere on your site,

00:05:56.812 --> 00:05:59.320
kind of just like
Google Analytics would.

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:01.450
And because of that,
there's many more use cases

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:03.820
that we want to enable
enterprises, you all,

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:06.340
to attune your business to and
to attune your fraud and risk

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:07.370
teams to.

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:09.982
And so we added higher
granularity risk scores.

00:06:09.982 --> 00:06:11.440
So rather than four
scores, you get

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:14.137
10 reason codes that'll
tell you why we thought

00:06:14.137 --> 00:06:16.720
something on your site was high
risk or something on your site

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:18.080
might be worth looking at.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:19.930
And then an
annotation API, which

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:22.060
is a means by which you
can help us tune our model

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:24.340
and tune our protection
to your particular site

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:25.760
and your particular use case.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.480
So we can get higher accuracy
and higher granularity

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:32.668
on our defenses for your own
site and your own business.

00:06:32.668 --> 00:06:34.210
So just with a higher
granularity use

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:35.752
score, kind of one
example of one way

00:06:35.752 --> 00:06:38.470
to think about it is if you
have very low granularity,

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:40.880
you can do defenses of
very different use cases.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:42.490
For example,
defending a login page

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:43.720
versus defending a home page.

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:45.460
If you defend a
home page, maybe you

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.050
allow some questionable
transactions through,

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:48.730
or maybe you don't care
at all if you don't

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:49.980
care if bots scrape your site.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:52.192
Many retailers we work
with, that's the case.

00:06:52.192 --> 00:06:53.650
Whereas very few
people want anyone

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:55.930
scraping or having automated
uses of their login page.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:57.890
That's generally a bad thing.

00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:00.100
Now, that would be good
if you have this the four

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.350
buckets and that as that--
what that was designed for.

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:04.690
With higher granularity,
with these 10 buckets,

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.350
you can draw even
finer controls.

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:09.520
For example, the way you treat
threats against a password

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:11.333
reset form versus a login form.

00:07:11.333 --> 00:07:13.750
Maybe those two are different
vectors and different levels

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:14.680
of security.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:17.380
And you can start making these
really fine-tune controls

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:20.200
and tuning that true positive,
false positive, false negative

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:22.610
rate for every specific
part of your business.

00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:25.145
So you can ensure that you
maximize the friction again

00:07:25.145 --> 00:07:26.770
for those attackers
and you minimize it

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:31.450
for your users or legitimate
folks trying to use your site.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.940
Along that same lines,
we have our reason codes.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:35.480
And here are just a few.

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:37.690
And again, going back to
maybe the scraping example

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.220
with automation.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.697
If we identify something
as an automation attack,

00:07:41.697 --> 00:07:43.780
maybe it doesn't matter
if it's on your home page.

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:44.920
Maybe you don't
care if folks are

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:46.430
scraping the basic
information you'd

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:47.650
like the whole world to know.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:50.380
But rarely would you want
to see that on a login page

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:52.420
or potentially, like,
a sending message

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:56.392
page or various other avenues
for abuse within your site.

00:07:56.392 --> 00:07:58.600
And then the other two
patterns are just ways for you

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:01.900
to potentially identify
different behaviors

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:03.860
that you wouldn't want
to see on your site.

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:05.652
So, for example, the
unexpected environment

00:08:05.652 --> 00:08:08.080
indicates that their reCAPTCHA
snippet has been extracted.

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:10.890
And that's a common way
that these reCAPTCHA farmers

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.520
will extract the
reCAPTCHA snippet

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:15.670
into a different environment
and have it solved externally.

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:19.930
Typically not a good thing,
not being used as intended.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:21.910
As well as the unexpected
usage patterns, which

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:24.243
could be any wide variety of
things, where you say, hey,

00:08:24.243 --> 00:08:26.740
this doesn't match the
typical legitimate behavior

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:30.910
we see for users on
your site on this page.

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:32.530
Again, we make it
really, really hard,

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:34.809
where the adversaries to
defeat this are starting

00:08:34.809 --> 00:08:37.809
to have to map to not
only typical users, not

00:08:37.809 --> 00:08:39.340
only to your site,
but specifically

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:42.100
to the behavior that would
be expected on your site

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:44.950
on your page, which makes it
a much, much tougher defense

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:49.543
and also much easier
on your users.

00:08:49.543 --> 00:08:51.460
And then the last piece
here is the annotation

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:53.420
or the annotate API call.

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:55.102
So when you use
reCAPTCHA, it'll send

00:08:55.102 --> 00:08:56.310
you back a score and a label.

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:57.275
So again, that score.

00:08:57.275 --> 00:08:58.900
There's 10 scores as
well as the labels

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:01.958
that we showed before as
well as-- and then when

00:09:01.958 --> 00:09:04.000
you receive those, you
can annotate them and send

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:05.792
them back to further
help train this model.

00:09:05.792 --> 00:09:09.157
Something we heard
continuously is that we really

00:09:09.157 --> 00:09:10.990
would like to share
ground truth with Google

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:13.240
and really help use the
ground truth that you see

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:15.640
in your business to help
us create a model that's

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:19.460
particular and tailored to your
business and to your company.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:21.265
And this will enable
us to do that.

00:09:21.265 --> 00:09:22.283
And here's how it works.

00:09:22.283 --> 00:09:23.950
It looks quite simple,
but basically you

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:27.298
just take the assessment that
you're given back from Google.

00:09:27.298 --> 00:09:28.840
As you think about
implementing this,

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:30.007
be sure to save that number.

00:09:30.007 --> 00:09:31.490
It's like your kind of receipt.

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:33.252
And then use that
to send us back

00:09:33.252 --> 00:09:35.710
a note that says, well, this
was a legitimate or fraudulent

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:36.220
transaction.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:37.510
And you can do both.

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:38.650
And you can do it for
whether we're right

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:39.608
or whether we're wrong.

00:09:39.608 --> 00:09:41.830
All will help us train
and label our data sets

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:43.850
to get better attuned
to your specific sites.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:46.100
Rather than, again, being
served by this general model

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:49.480
of the entire web, we can start
using all of our protections

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:53.560
and knowledge to tailor a
model specific to your site.

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:56.495
And just a little bit for folks
who may already be V3 users.

00:09:56.495 --> 00:09:58.870
I actually can't see, but how
many people in the audience

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:02.088
are V3 users already?

00:10:02.088 --> 00:10:02.880
That's pretty good.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:04.190
I see four or five hands go up.

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:06.440
By the way, this is the
product team in the front row.

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:09.220
All the head snapped
round of intense interest.

00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:12.230
So the folks who are in V3
or any version of reCAPTCHA,

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:15.340
really the only change you
have to make is-- let's see,

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:17.230
this thing doesn't
laser point, does it?

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:18.970
