00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:10.110
And the last product we'll
talk about today is web risk.

00:19:10.110 --> 00:19:12.690
And web risk is
essentially a way

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:14.850
to protect you from
malicious URLs.

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:17.920
We all know that URLs can
contain dangerous stuff.

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:20.790
You know, phishing, malware,
all sorts of bad stuff.

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:24.030
And Safe Browsing examines more
than a billion URLs every day

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:28.110
in order to create a list
of a million or more URLs.

00:19:28.110 --> 00:19:30.707
And really, it's access to that
list that we're providing now.

00:19:30.707 --> 00:19:33.040
And here's an example of maybe
how can work in practice.

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:36.120
So let's say there's
a rub site, Acme Tech

00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:38.340
Reviews for tech events
in San Francisco,

00:19:38.340 --> 00:19:40.410
like Google Cloud Next.

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:41.517
And it gets more popular.

00:19:41.517 --> 00:19:43.350
But as it gets more
popular, you see a bunch

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:44.350
of this malware come up.

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:46.740
And this is actually a very
common trending behavior

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:47.550
we see.

00:19:47.550 --> 00:19:50.340
As sites, as businesses
hit this inflection point,

00:19:50.340 --> 00:19:52.830
where they attract users who
are becoming really popular,

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:54.450
we see the fraud come
right along with it.

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:56.700
So rides right on the coattails
of your success, which

00:19:56.700 --> 00:19:58.570
is often quite frustrating.

00:19:58.570 --> 00:20:00.510
And then it kind of dampens it.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:02.872
So as that site
gets more popular,

00:20:02.872 --> 00:20:04.830
attracts more malicious
content that showing up

00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:06.622
on the site, it starts
to drive users away,

00:20:06.622 --> 00:20:09.038
which is bad for that business
and bad for that business's

00:20:09.038 --> 00:20:09.660
growth.

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:13.230
And so really with the Web Risk
API, what this business, Acme

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:16.320
Tech Reviews, could do is
send good and bad URLs,

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:19.030
all URLs posted to its
site, to the Web Risk API

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:21.030
to check to see if they're
known to be malicious

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:23.570
or known to be unsafe or not.

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:25.340
With the Web Risk API
will send the data

00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:29.210
on known unsafe or known bad
URLs back to the Acme Tech

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:29.972
Reviews site.

00:20:29.972 --> 00:20:31.430
And then Acme Tech
Reviews can only

00:20:31.430 --> 00:20:33.290
post the URLs that
were not found

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:35.690
to be bad to the
actual public site,

00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:37.790
and that way make
sure its content is

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:39.620
a lot safer and more secure.

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:42.110
And then its users aren't being
targeted by the propagation

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:43.430
of malicious content.

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:47.160
And here's really quickly what
the queries will look like.

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:48.433
There's two basic methods.

00:20:48.433 --> 00:20:50.100
One is you can
essentially submit a URL,

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:54.220
and that's the one on your left.

00:20:54.220 --> 00:20:58.200
And submit a URL, get a
verdict back, pretty simple.

00:20:58.200 --> 00:20:59.780
The other one
essentially consists

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:02.270
of a local database
of partial hashes

00:21:02.270 --> 00:21:03.860
you can run queries against.

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:06.200
And when there's a query
match, we'll send back.

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:08.100
And you can see
that on the right,

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:10.850
you can see a list of
different URLs and they match.

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:12.980
This is not only
faster, but it's also

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:15.312
privacy preserving because
Google never actually sees

00:21:15.312 --> 00:21:16.520
the URL you were looking for.

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:20.090
We only see a set of possible
URLs you might be looking for,

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:22.340
you might be interested in.

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:25.790
As you know here, expire time
will kind of denote the time

00:21:25.790 --> 00:21:27.380
for which we would like we--

00:21:27.380 --> 00:21:30.230
our terms encourage you
consider the URLs unsafe.

00:21:30.230 --> 00:21:32.280
And the negative
expire time is the time

00:21:32.280 --> 00:21:34.280
which we discourage you
from making another call

00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:36.230
because it's unlikely
the verdict will change,

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:37.520
even if there is no verdict.

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:39.745
So kind of consider
it like, you know,

00:21:39.745 --> 00:21:41.120
don't ask again
for a little bit.

00:21:43.520 --> 00:21:45.020
I'm going to go
back to our example.

00:21:45.020 --> 00:21:46.780
So now let's say Acme
Reviews has installed

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:48.400
this, and it's starting
to filter their sites.

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:49.775
What will happen
is they'll start

00:21:49.775 --> 00:21:52.580
to make sure that their site
is free of malicious content

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:54.930
and the users return and
their growth can continue.

00:21:54.930 --> 00:21:58.250
So for any company that
does content filtering, has

00:21:58.250 --> 00:22:00.950
large amounts of
user-generated content,

00:22:00.950 --> 00:22:04.167
highly encourage them to take
a look at this Web Risk API.

00:22:04.167 --> 00:22:05.750
We actually launched
this back at RSA,

00:22:05.750 --> 00:22:07.292
so this is the one
product that's up.

00:22:07.292 --> 00:22:11.215
You can go look on it now at
cloud.google.com/web-risk.

00:22:11.215 --> 00:22:13.340
And again, we have data on
more than a million URLs

00:22:13.340 --> 00:22:16.980
from scanning billions a day.

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:19.520
And I wanted to just
close quickly here

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:24.077
with a discussion of how this
fits together as a hijacking

00:22:24.077 --> 00:22:24.910
prevention use case.

00:22:24.910 --> 00:22:27.640
So fraud, and just
attacks in general,

00:22:27.640 --> 00:22:29.860
things that are self
propagating and work together.

00:22:29.860 --> 00:22:33.250
Someone phishes a user,
steals a password,

00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:35.750
tries it on a website through
automated credential stuffing,

00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:37.730
or even manual
credential stuffing,

00:22:37.730 --> 00:22:40.487
and then it's-- that compromised
site is used to re-post more

00:22:40.487 --> 00:22:41.570
phishing and more malware.

00:22:41.570 --> 00:22:44.573
And that negative,
malicious cycle continues.

00:22:44.573 --> 00:22:46.490
We really designed this
suite to work together

00:22:46.490 --> 00:22:48.715
to block every
step of that cycle.

00:22:48.715 --> 00:22:50.090
So phishing
protection's designed

00:22:50.090 --> 00:22:51.932
to stop users from
clicking on phishing

00:22:51.932 --> 00:22:54.140
to ensure that they are--
the passwords aren't stolen

00:22:54.140 --> 00:22:54.843
the first place.

00:22:54.843 --> 00:22:57.260
We have reCAPTCHA enterprise,
and among many other things,

00:22:57.260 --> 00:22:59.552
will stop credential stuffing,
and stop those passwords

00:22:59.552 --> 00:23:01.903
from being used, even
if they are compromised

00:23:01.903 --> 00:23:03.320
or, at very least,
giving you some

00:23:03.320 --> 00:23:05.700
notice that people are
using these in an attack.

00:23:05.700 --> 00:23:07.730
And then finally, we
have Web Risk, which

00:23:07.730 --> 00:23:10.220
prevents the propagation
of phishing and malware

00:23:10.220 --> 00:23:11.990
through these large
user-content sites

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:15.670
and through any sort of
security filtering systems,

00:23:15.670 --> 00:23:18.350
be it email or anything
else, to ensure

00:23:18.350 --> 00:23:20.040
that even if the
site is compromised,

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:22.430
it doesn't start spreading
to the rest of our ecosystem.

00:23:22.430 --> 00:23:26.080
[MUSIC PLAYING]

